    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0770" n="650" xml:id="pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.6511 Grandi, Dino/149: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-11T11:00:00-05:00">December 11, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>161. Your 234<anchor n="39" xml:id="d674-f1"/> and 235, December 10. I appreciate
                    very much Minister Grandi’s courtesy in giving you in advance an English
                    translation of his speech regarding his visit to the United States. The generous
                    and friendly tone of Signor Grandi’s remarks cannot fail to make a good
                    impression in the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
